WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.740
Whether these are five-star luxury suites
or seedy roach motels, there’s something

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:09.190
undeniably a little eerie about hotels.

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:14.290
They’re liminal spaces - transitional spots
between origins and destinations.

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:19.900
We’ve seen countless creepy hotel rooms
in the horror genre, from Room 237 in The

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:24.920
Shining’s Overlook Hotel to the infamous
Room 1408.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:28.250
But have you ever heard of Room 710?

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:32.870
Also known by a different number: SCP-2432.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:38.010
This hotel room is one of the most terrifying
out there, but the funny thing is, you won’t

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:40.090
ever hear a bad word said about it.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:45.800
Room 710 has glowing - if a little strangely-worded
- reviews across the board.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:50.290
And when you see how people rave about it
online, you’ll find yourself unable to resist

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:51.470
paying it a visit.

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:53.100
But don’t be nervous.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.460
All those people can’t be wrong, right?

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:58.250
And after all, it’s just a room.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:00.870
What kind of harm could a room really do?

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:06.600
Let’s ask Chuck Peele, one of the many victims
of SCP-2432.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:11.240
He was a traveling businessman, caught in
the rat race of relentless sales pitches and

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:15.810
conferences that felt like they were slowly
but surely sucking out his soul.

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:19.939
His next conference was in State College,
Pennsylvania, and he’d spent the evening

00:01:19.939 --> 00:01:23.939
researching different places he could potentially
stay during the trip.

00:01:23.939 --> 00:01:28.880
Chuck had been disenchanted with chain hotels
over the years - seeing the exact same setups

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:33.930
again and again, all across the country, only
worsened the feeling that his life was going

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:34.930
nowhere.

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:39.149
That’s why, whenever he was traveling out
of town, he always tried to find an interesting

00:01:39.149 --> 00:01:41.359
independent place to hang his hat.

00:01:41.359 --> 00:01:44.819
That’s what led him to the [REDACTED] Hotel.

00:01:44.819 --> 00:01:49.700
The pictures seemed nice, sure, but what really
caught his eye were the positively fantastic

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:50.700
reviews.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:54.920
Little note: Certain details have been redacted
to avoid subjecting you, the viewer, to the

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:58.130
memetic effects nested in these reviews.

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:02.539
After all, we wouldn’t want you to develop
a sudden hankering for Room 710, and start

00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:05.419
buying your tickets to State College, Pennsylvania.

00:02:05.419 --> 00:02:10.190
The first review, found on Trip Advisor, said:
“Another great stay in this fabulous hotel!

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:14.180
The room was perfect, the staff friendly as
always, and of course no better location than

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:15.829
on the plane of many hives.

00:02:15.829 --> 00:02:20.181
I have enjoyed a drink at the friendly bar,
this time I added a wonderful escape and the

00:02:20.181 --> 00:02:22.040
breakfast was cold and the breakfast was warm.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:23.040
Another great stay in this fabulous hotel!

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:27.829
The restaurant has lovely ambiance and the
food was over the top alive and kicking woo!

00:02:27.829 --> 00:02:29.090
Would stifle again.

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:32.480
My husband eats out often and felt this was
the best one ever.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:34.849
Another great stay in this fabulous hotel!

00:02:34.849 --> 00:02:37.609
One more great item to add to the [REDACTED.]

00:02:37.609 --> 00:02:39.780
Another great stay in this fabulous hotel!

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:42.980
Stayed July 1999, traveled with three family
members.”

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:45.909
The second review, this time posted on Yelp,
read:

00:02:45.909 --> 00:02:50.130
“We sailed on our boat into State College
from outside State College through the night

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:53.440
and the cold and arrived at 8am in State College.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:58.150
The hotel desk staff allowed us to check in
at 8am in the evening with our sixty four

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:02.810
young boys - this was absolutely AWESOME awesome
customer service!

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:07.989
We cannot thank you enough for allowing us
to check in so early in State College.

00:03:07.989 --> 00:03:09.099
Earlier then war.

00:03:09.099 --> 00:03:13.959
The rest of the stay was fine - we spent almost
all of our time in the room; mostly just to

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:14.959
sleep.

00:03:14.959 --> 00:03:19.420
This location is ultra ultra convenient with
downtown downtown State College and allowed

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:24.280
me to make a midnight run for some of my favorite
State College meat while the family was sleeping

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:29.269
and sleeping and sleeping and sleeeeping in
State College.

00:03:29.269 --> 00:03:30.269
Downtown.

00:03:30.269 --> 00:03:32.150
[REDACTED] Downtown.”

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:36.079
And the final review, which Chuck Peele found
particularly compelling, read:

00:03:36.079 --> 00:03:39.129
“Been coming to this region for fourteen
stone.

00:03:39.129 --> 00:03:40.129
What a blast.

00:03:40.129 --> 00:03:43.590
Scores of humans wondering the streets and
staffing the hotel.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:47.310
My husband and my husband and I have walked
drooling path to get here.

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:52.950
Bed in Room 710 was soft and cosy and appreciated
the decor would recommend the bed and specifically

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:55.140
the bed and specifically the bed.

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:59.190
[REDACTED] in the pool and it was lovely,
crisp blue hydrogen and you could see all

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:02.180
of the people relax into a meandering menace.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:03.299
Towel slightly dirty.

00:04:03.299 --> 00:04:07.390
Gym was full of usable equipment, so you could
train not in fear.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:09.379
And the local wildlife was remarkable.

00:04:09.379 --> 00:04:15.139
I visited the town in the past and have never
seen so many puma being feasted on [REDACTED]

00:04:15.139 --> 00:04:18.400
and the toucan-men were especially numerous
today.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:22.130
Arrived July 2019, staying three days months
ten years.”

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:26.340
While these may seem like utter nonsense to
you, to someone reading them without the key

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:32.020
memetic trigger phrases redacted, they create
an irresistible urge to visit the hotel and

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:34.389
stay in Room 710.

00:04:34.389 --> 00:04:39.490
It was an urge so primal and powerful that
he couldn’t wait to get going, if only because

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:44.130
he could finally stay in this wonderful hotel
and see what all this fuss was about.

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:49.270
He booked his tickets, and a few days later,
he was at the check-in desk.

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:54.669
Something you need to understand is that Room
710 is extremely subtle in its anomalous methods.

00:04:54.669 --> 00:05:01.580
Unlike Room 237 or Room 1408, it won’t attack
the victim with ghosts or mind-warping hallucinations.

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:06.770
Nor will it drive them into acts of horrific
violence against the ones they love, or acts

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:08.639
of self-destruction.

00:05:08.639 --> 00:05:13.300
One of the frightening things about Room 710
is that, while you’re actually inside it,

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:15.710
you can have an extremely pleasant stay.

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:19.260
It’s only once you leave that things start
becoming truly terrifying.

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:22.030
But we’ll get to that when we get to it.

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:25.990
Chuck made his way up to the room to take
a shower and take the weight off his feet.

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:31.500
And sure enough, the room seemed positively
luxurious: Two queen-sized beds with fine

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:37.060
linen, a spacious closet, a large flatscreen
television, and a well-appointed bathroom

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:39.300
with a combo shower-bath.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:40.729
This was heaven.

00:05:40.729 --> 00:05:44.690
Sure, it was one more bed than he needed,
but this meant he had a choice of which one

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:46.810
he could sleep on.

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:48.230
Fantastic!

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:51.129
This is the insidious power of SCP-2432.

00:05:51.129 --> 00:05:55.229
There’s nothing overt about the harm it
causes at first.

00:05:55.229 --> 00:05:59.070
Chuck was more worried about the impending
conference than he was about the fact he was

00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:01.240
in the belly of the anomalous beast.

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:06.669
However, the SCP Foundation, through later
analysis of the room, found that the anomalous

00:06:06.669 --> 00:06:11.910
elements aren’t entirely ephemeral - there
are certain details about the physical makeup

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:15.840
of the room that causes and amplifies its
effects.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:20.250
The walls are reinforced with hyper-strong
aramid fibers, and it’s believed that the

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:25.240
very makeup of the room serves to create mind-warping
oscillations that are undetectable to the

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:30.860
conscious mind, but are particularly potent
when the victim is asleep.

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:35.870
Chuck didn’t know it, but every moment he
spent in that room, it was crawling into his

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:38.580
head just that little bit more.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:43.410
He was already subconsciously composing his
nonsensical memetic review of the place.

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:47.979
As the night drew to a close, Chuck decided
to relax and enjoy some television.

00:06:47.979 --> 00:06:51.539
The hotel’s website boasted a wide variety
of channels, after all.

00:06:51.539 --> 00:06:55.800
But after switching through a few different
channels, he came to rest at a channel simply

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:57.729
called “roomnews.”

00:06:57.729 --> 00:07:03.350
It was simple but soothing: An image of a
sailboat in the middle of a pastoral lake,

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:06.419
while what sounded like cheerful elevator
music played.

00:07:06.419 --> 00:07:11.450
Chuck simply sat and enjoyed the relaxing
ambiance for a moment, before the music was

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:17.069
interrupted by a deep, British voice, who
began delivering a strange monologue.

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:22.240
For reasons he couldn’t quite explain, Chuck
felt that this voice was speaking directly

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:23.240
to him.

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:26.160
“Let me describe something to you.

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:28.070
This is a true story.

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:30.030
It really happened to me.

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:32.980
It could have happened to you.

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:38.259
Every day you wake up and you go to your job
and there’s just something off about your

00:07:38.259 --> 00:07:41.750
boss, he’s weird and clingy and strange.

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:45.229
Your co-workers are nice enough but they don’t
communicate.

00:07:45.229 --> 00:07:52.090
They are quiet and out of it and absorbed
in their own little worlds and you are ignored.

00:07:52.090 --> 00:07:57.650
Not because you are ugly or awkward or rude
but because you are there.

00:07:57.650 --> 00:08:01.330
And you suspect things about your co-workers.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:06.449
Despite their habits and the strange things
each of them places on their Twitter pages

00:08:06.449 --> 00:08:10.470
they seem to be doing so much better than
you.

00:08:10.470 --> 00:08:12.979
How are you falling behind?

00:08:12.979 --> 00:08:15.129
And you should love the job.

00:08:15.129 --> 00:08:17.539
It’s your passion.

00:08:17.539 --> 00:08:21.509
Most would die to be doing a job they are
passionate about.

00:08:21.509 --> 00:08:24.820
You really should but you can’t.

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:32.400
Wonder becomes routine and routine becomes
drudgery and it’s day in and day out and

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:36.200
you struggle to maintain your soul.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:39.090
This is not what should happen.

00:08:39.090 --> 00:08:41.890
'Should' is such a tormenting word.

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:43.550
A thinking trap.

00:08:43.550 --> 00:08:44.550
Should.

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:47.110
Your life is ruled by shoulds.

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:52.900
You come home in your beat-up old car along
the same boring street in your town.

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:58.120
Everything is along that main drag and you
cannot really go elsewhere.

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:03.780
Everything is overcast and the pedestrians
are idiots and the drivers are too.

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:08.030
You get home and have a million, billion projects
to accomplish.

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:12.060
You should compete in the rat race but you’re
bone tired.

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:16.560
You promise your grandmother you should text
her because she’s going through chemo and

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:21.550
she only just figured out texting because
she’s getting old and having a hard time

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:29.540
adjusting and it’s so painful for her and
you should be there but the job is so demanding.

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:32.200
You have a thousand books you should be reading.

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:34.720
You have a million projects you should complete.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:39.960
The rent on your tiny apartment is due and
the dishes are piling high and dirty in the

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:40.960
sink.

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:45.680
You barely have enough money for pizza as
you lie in your boxers on your greasy 10-year-old

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:50.410
couch from an IKEA in Fishkill, New York that
closed a year ago.

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:53.320
You remember your mom taking you there as
a kid.

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:55.140
Then she left.

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:58.550
You feel a deep, growing anxiety.

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:04.030
The feeling of watching your life burn around
you as you try and try to succeed for something

00:10:04.030 --> 00:10:10.720
great, to make your mark on society but you
cannot bring yourself to do so despite your

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:11.720
convictions.

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:13.510
The dread is horrible.

00:10:13.510 --> 00:10:16.040
It’s all crumbling apart.

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:20.530
The parade is passing you by and you are helpless.

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:26.900
Immobile in your state like a great boulder
made of disappointment, regret, depression

00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:29.380
and malaise.

00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:32.070
There is nothing for you here.

00:10:32.070 --> 00:10:34.970
You need to leave this place.

00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:37.770
You have a choice.

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:43.460
Get your good clean shirt and your smart pants
and announce you are taking a break.

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:46.580
Don’t even pack, don’t even bring your
phone.

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:50.350
One simple call to the office and get on your
way.

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:54.870
Take that old beat-up car from the garage
underneath your apartment complex, give your

00:10:54.870 --> 00:10:58.940
cat the last of his food and some water, and
hit the road.

00:10:58.940 --> 00:11:03.520
Leave the town and your ex and the promises
you made and your job and your grandmother

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:06.710
and your responsibilities and worries.

00:11:06.710 --> 00:11:10.860
What I recommend to you is simple: Find a
hotel.

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:12.850
Not a motel or something shabby.

00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:14.030
A hotel.

00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:16.000
Even a chain will do.

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:17.880
Hotels are simply remarkable, aren’t they?

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:19.950
Clean and elegant.

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:22.770
All modernistic and designed to appeal to
the eye.

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:25.910
You don’t need to care about a thing in
the world.

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:32.050
Food is provided, they clean up after you
and you can feel like you have some luxury

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:33.510
for once.

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:38.940
Most even have pools and fitness centers where
you can finally get in shape and pick your

00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:39.940
life up.

00:11:39.940 --> 00:11:43.370
It’s a chance to step back and regroup.

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:45.710
Take a look at the customers around you.

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:47.450
Travelers, most.

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:50.100
Strange people, interesting people.

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:52.850
People you won’t ever see again.

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:56.420
Travel is so romantic, so mysterious.

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:59.870
My, what stories these people probably have!

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:05.020
And the staff, also all so attentive in their
smart little uniforms.

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:07.340
Don’t listen to the naysayers.

00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:10.140
These people all love their jobs.

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:11.610
You know they do.

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:14.020
The room is amazing.

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:18.530
The wallpaper is elegant and the paintings
make you feel at ease.

00:12:18.530 --> 00:12:22.920
There are clean towels every day and the bed
is freshly made.

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:25.940
You can escape the oncoming storm outside.

00:12:25.940 --> 00:12:29.520
The thunder crashing down on the roof like
ball bearings.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:32.570
You could live your whole life in this place.

00:12:32.570 --> 00:12:34.940
Enjoy the sugary cereals at the breakfast
buffet.

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:37.900
Get a loyalty card and pay no money.

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:40.620
Travel really changes a man.

00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:41.820
Relaxes him.

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:44.460
Shapes him up into a better person.

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:48.490
You become a better person by staying in a
hotel.

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:52.050
Strong, social, a proper soldier.

00:12:52.050 --> 00:12:54.410
You adapt to the hotel mindset.

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:57.710
Enjoy the soft music and eat that fresh waffle.

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:02.540
Grab a beer in the evening with your fellow
transients from the attached sports bar.

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:06.300
Relax and watch that old showing of that superhero
movie on your TV.

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:08.500
Live here forever.

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:10.170
Enjoy the hotel.

00:13:10.170 --> 00:13:11.880
Become the hotel.

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:12.880
Never leave.

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:14.600
Why would you want to leave?

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:19.040
Even when you do walk out those pristine glass
sliding doors, you are empty.

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:23.830
The hotel is in your soul now and you feel
a worse person away from it.

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:27.430
You feel yourself slipping back to that grey
life.

00:13:27.430 --> 00:13:30.810
A black hole is in your heart.

00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:33.230
Your soul is the hotel.

00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:36.100
Your consciousness is the hotel.

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:39.190
You are now one with your accommodations.

00:13:39.190 --> 00:13:42.610
You are your accommodations are your life.

00:13:42.610 --> 00:13:43.610
Ascend.

00:13:43.610 --> 00:13:46.050
Isn’t that lovely?”

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:48.590
As he fell asleep, Chuck found himself nodding.

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:50.630
Yes, yes, that is lovely.

00:13:50.630 --> 00:13:53.160
How nice it would be to ascend.

00:13:53.160 --> 00:14:00.160
Little did he know, he was receiving a broadcast
from SCP-2432-1, a small, boil-like creature

00:14:00.160 --> 00:14:02.850
affixed to the back of the television.

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:07.590
Foundation tests have revealed that this creature
is made from a mix of human, rockfish, and

00:14:07.590 --> 00:14:09.170
pig-like DNA.

00:14:09.170 --> 00:14:14.330
It only causes strange broadcasts when affixed
to the back of this particular television.

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:15.460
But that’s fine.

00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:17.040
Chuck rather enjoyed the show.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:18.830
It gave him a lot to think about…

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:24.240
He left the hotel a changed man a few days
later, once the conference was finally over,

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:26.180
and gave it a glowing review.

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:30.760
It was not long after he’d returned home
that he began to notice the changes taking

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:31.760
place.

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:37.030
Nothing extreme at first - just gaining some
weight, and then, a little stranger, he began

00:14:37.030 --> 00:14:40.820
to develop a purple rash that just wouldn’t
go away.

00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:44.980
As the rash worsened, it seemed to take on
almost a floral pattern.

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:46.260
Chuck didn’t mind.

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:49.900
If ever you asked him, he’d just murmur
something about “ascending.”

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:52.680
Then the changes got worse.

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:57.020
A television-shaped protrusion made from bone
began to grow in Chuck’s stomach.

00:14:57.020 --> 00:15:00.010
His intestines became rickety porcelain pipes.

00:15:00.010 --> 00:15:03.300
His liver turned into a plush, well-fluffed
pillow.

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:08.300
His muscles began to take on a similar quality
to the aramid fibers in the walls of Room

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:09.560
710.

00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:11.530
But he still didn’t mind.

00:15:11.530 --> 00:15:15.060
As he got bigger and bigger, he didn’t mind.

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:20.410
As his organs and bones transformed into furniture
inside him, he didn’t mind.

00:15:20.410 --> 00:15:26.350
He didn’t even mind when his body got so
large that it formed a roughly cube-like shape.

00:15:26.350 --> 00:15:29.320
In fact, he couldn’t be happier.

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:31.190
He was just like that room.

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:33.880
That beautiful, wonderful room.

00:15:33.880 --> 00:15:39.110
Just like the man on the television said:
He was now one with the accommodation, and

00:15:39.110 --> 00:15:40.850
he couldn’t be happier.

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:44.390
He’d never much enjoyed being a human, anyway…

00:15:44.390 --> 00:15:48.850
Such is the fate of everyone who stays in
SCP-2432 eventually.

00:15:48.850 --> 00:15:54.630
You’ll love the room so much that eventually,
you’ll start emulating it.

00:15:54.630 --> 00:15:58.600
Sure, that may seem frightening now, but don’t
worry.

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:03.920
On the other end of the transformation, you’ll
be much more...accomodating.

00:16:03.920 --> 00:16:10.231
Now go check out “SCP-3082 - Neverland's
Lost Boys and Girls” and “SCP-1730 - What

00:16:10.231 --> 00:16:11.231
Happened to Site-13?

00:16:11.231 --> 00:16:16.550
The Full Story Compilation” for more journeys
into terrifying anomalous locations!

